From 96b9c66acfb169a95ee7dfebd1522410ecb20dfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ramon Kaspar <ramonkaspar@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 70/72] NeMo Gym: token ids of a turn without new prompt tokens
 stay integers

torch.tensor of an empty list is float32. A later turn of a multi-turn
rollout can add no prompt tokens to the tokens so far: 4 of the 512
rollouts of a ToolGrow step had such a turn, at step 33 of a Chonk run.
The user message of such a turn then had float32 token ids and loss
mask, and batched_message_log_to_flat_message stopped the training loop
with "expected consistent types". These token ids are now int64.

A turn without generated tokens needs no change: the loop skips it.
---
 nemo_rl/environments/nemo_gym.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/nemo_rl/environments/nemo_gym.py b/nemo_rl/environments/nemo_gym.py
index 30588e4f4..991477dfa 100644
--- a/nemo_rl/environments/nemo_gym.py
+++ b/nemo_rl/environments/nemo_gym.py
@@ -1275,7 +1275,7 @@ output prompt token ids till seen: {output_item_dict["prompt_token_ids"][: len(s
             user_message = {
                 "role": "user",
                 "content": "",
-                "token_ids": torch.tensor(new_prompt_token_ids),
+                "token_ids": torch.tensor(new_prompt_token_ids, dtype=torch.long),
             }
             if routed_experts is not None:
                 user_message["routed_experts"] = routed_experts[prompt_start:prompt_end]
